:: "Be a good man." You know you have to do something about it. {"position":"1050,650","size":"100,100"}
I will kill him
For my vows and
For millions of people like her.

You made up your mind, but you knew it will be a tough road.
You waited almost a year to seize opportunies.
Finally,
Next Monday is the king's 20th nameday. And he will be showing himself in the king's road in the midtown. A royal progress.

This is it,
You told yourself.

But you will need help.
The king's strongest guard and knight, Sir Gawain, is with him 24/7 almost. It is told that he is invincible.
You got to know a lot of people in these years of wars. There are two of them you think you can trust:

[[Gate, a smith that you know from Vandes villiage, he could the build the finest armor for you. We could strike him during the parade.]]

[[Vane, A facemaker...that you once captured during the war and you set him free. He promised he will help you in any situation. You just saw him yesterday in the inn. Maybe he could think of something...]]

[["Maybe I should get a family like she once said..."]]


:: "How did I get here?" {"position":"1100,400","size":"100,100"}
"Oh right, a fleabag. I was born there"

Stinky, crowded, noisy,
And of course, hungry.
That was all you can recall.

You try to picture the faces of your mom and dad, but it does not work.
It never did. 
At least for the first 10 years.

But she found you there.
She was already pregnant when she found you being beaten up in the street corner. You were skinny, mud on your face. She came close, broke the bread at her hand in half and slowly offered me. Her hands were shaking, probably afraid of me. Right...I could relate if I was her. 

She used to work at a brothel near the skid row. A lot of powerful men came by everyday to have fun without being found by their wives. But she accidentally caught a disease from one of them. They abandoned her, because she can no longer work. 

She gave me a home ever since, even though that means another mouth to feed.
The word "mom", has a face then.

The life was tough, 
Luckily we got each other.
You once asked her, 
"Do we have a dad?"
"Once, but he will never come back."
You never asked further, you are smart.

[["I will not let them suffer..."]]


:: "I am grateful for that. But no. That is not my place to be." {"position":"2050,1475","size":"100,100"}
“I am grateful.
But no.
That is not my place to be.”

You waited for anger.
For the guards to step forward.
For the Queen to remind you that you had no right to refuse.

Instead,
Gwyneth smiled.

Her shoulders relaxed.
Beside her, the Queen closed her eyes and let out a long breath.

“May I ask why?” Gwyneth said.

You looked at the crown.

“Because I want it.
And I am afraid of how much.”

She took her mother’s hand.
They were both smiling now.

“Then there is something I want to show you.”


For years, Gwyneth had been filling notebooks with a question nobody dared to ask:

What happens when the King is wrong?

Her answer lay across three sheets of parchment.

“A parliament to make the laws.
A king to carry them out.
Independent courts to judge by them.”

“Three rulers?” you asked.

“Three powers. Each with limits the others can enforce.”

She called it the separation of powers.

“And who chooses the King?”

She handed you the unfinished page.

“We do.
All of us.”

At first, you waited for someone to draw a sword.

Then you learned to listen for the vote.

Greed had survived.
But it could no longer have everything it wanted.

One winter evening,
you saw a woman leaving the public kitchen.

An infant slept in her arms.
Beside her, a thin child carried a loaf of bread.

He broke it in half.
The larger piece went to his mother.

You knew that gesture.

Gwyneth found you standing there,
your face wet with tears.

“Do you regret refusing?”

You shook your head.

That night, beside the fireplace,
you remembered your brother's cute face and
Your mother’s tired hands.

You wished you could tell her,

“We are doing better, Mom.”


[[GOOD ENDING]]


:: "I will not let them suffer..." {"position":"1250,425","size":"100,100"}
Five years past,
You are taller than her now.

Three years ago, your brother did not make it through that flee. Her condition is worse one day after another. 
She knew her time was close,
So was you.

"Get a family
Live your life. 
Take this sword, and
Be a good man."
That was her last words.

You were recruited to the battlefield a year after, fighting their war. You swing that sword to the battle. You slayed thousands of enimies with it. That sword, she told you it once belongs to a knight. A famous one.

You are stronger than anyone else.
He were given the title of a kinght not long during the war. For your kills, of course.

You made a vow,
"Be a good man."
You always remembered that.

[[But then the famine came...]]


:: "Maybe I should get a family like she once said..." {"position":"675,925","size":"100,100"}
You give up.
It is not your fault, it is not your responsibility either.
You told yourself that on that day.

You told yourself that on the day you met Marina.
You told yourself that on the day you get married.
You told yourself that on the day your son was born.
You told yourself that on the day you bought your first house.
You told yourself that on the day you moved to the east.
You told yourself that on the day your legs start to hurt.
You told yourself that on the day your sword start to get rusty.
You told yourself that on the day you can not get out of the bed.

You told yourself that on the last moment you died.

[[BAD ENDDING]] 


:: "Yes, I will take its price." {"position":"1150,900","size":"100,100"}
You looked at the mirror.
You can not believe yourself.
And you know there is no coming back.

You sneaked into the palace in the midnight before the parade. Because the kingsguard need to rest early that day so you know the real him will be asleep early. Nobody can tell you from the real Sir Gawain. You practiced well.

Now in front of you there are two rooms, you have to choose one.

[[Go to the King's bedroom]]

[[The Queen's bedroom with her children]]


:: BAD ENDDING {"position":"450,800","size":"100,100"}
Wanna Restart?

[[Childhood]] 


:: But then the famine came... [Fork1] {"position":"925,500","size":"100,100"}
Thousands of thousands,
they died of hunger.

But all he wants is conquer.
Authur IV
The Incompetent
The Notorious
The King

He has two children, the oldest Princess Gwyneth and the youger Prince Valerian. It is being said that Gwyneth is a wise women and she is 21 this year. She read a lot of books in law and politics. People all said she will be a fine queen. Sadly, she is a woman and Valerian just turned 18.

The king wants to take Umlandia, the wealthy neighbor country. He puts all the money in the vault for the war. Weapons, and horses. The rest of the money? 
Probably for wine and fun. 

[["Be a good man." You know you have to do something about it.]]


:: Childhood {"position":"700,375","size":"100,100"}
Cold
...You opened your eyes...
It seems that you just fell asleep, or maybe, almost...

A log is holding in your right hand, wet. The rest are lying in front of you.
Fireplace, you recognized it.

Some small sparks are jumping around like naughty elves, almost dazzling for your eyes in the rest of the darkness. It must be them that woke you up, you figured. 

[[You heard a baby crying behind you...]]





:: GOOD ENDING {"position":"1575,1600","size":"100,100"}
Wanna Restart?

[[Childhood]] 


:: Gate, a smith that you know from Vandes villiage, he could the build the finest armor for you. We could strike him during the parade. {"position":"775,600","size":"100,100"}
A silver armor with a flower on your chest,
"Perfect, this flower is for her."
You said this to yourself and wait till that day.

The parade is huge, thousands of people are here, it is crowded and chaotic. You knew it will be a good chance. Because it is hard to find you and good for you to disappear after the assassin.

You sezie the moment, jump quickly onto the carriage, and take out your sword. You strike at him but get blocked suddenly. It is him, Sir Gawain. You always knew this could happen, so you start to fight, but his sword is sharper than anything you have seen. After a few rounds, your armor are broken and there is a wound on your left leg. 

You can not get up again. He swing his sword in front of your face, and asks:

"Any last words?"

You suddenly realized,
his sword has exactly the same inscription and engraving as yours, 
"Protect the weak and the innocent."
How sarcastic?
The man mentioned by your mom,
It was him...

He put that sword down your throat, 
You fell,

You saw her face with your brother near the fireplace again,
only this time it is blurried by your tears.

"I am sorry, mom."

[[BAD ENDDING]]


:: Go to the King's bedroom {"position":"650,1100","size":"100,100"}
It is him.
But he is waiting for you.
So is Sir Gawain.
Vane snitched, it has to be him.
You have no way but to fight.

He is strong, just as the stories told. You knew this could be your only chance, so you fight will all the skills you have learnt during the war. But it is all for nothing. Your armor is way weaker than his and you are bleeding on both your arms and thighs in a few rounds. 

You can not get up again. He swing his sword in front of your face, and asks:

"Any last words?"

Vane knew,
his sword has exactly the same inscription and engraving as yours, 
"Protect the weak and the innocent."
How sarcastic?
The man mentioned by your mom,
It was him...

He put that sword down your throat, 
You fell,

You saw her face with your brother near the fireplace again,
only this time it is blurried by your tears.

"I am sorry, mom."

