:: Go to the King's bedroom - with Gwyneth and the Queen and Valerian died {"position":"1600,1325","size":"100,100"}
"Talk to him. Go into his room and lower his alarms. I will kill him once you come out. If you snitched to him, I will come insdie and kill all three of you."
The Queen has no other way but nods her head since you are putting a sword behind both of them. 
You let them in and waited at the doorstep of the King's bedroom.

Suddenly, the doors open, and the real Sir Gawain walks out. Standing outside the door and watching out for something. You are shocked and quickly hide behind a pillar. Why he is in King's room this late? Maybe he knows? And why the king sends him away just to talk to the Queen and her daughter? It must be something important or personal, you guessed.

He is not wearing a helmet. It is a good opportunity to launched a sneak attack against him. You realized. 
You sliently came close and use a heavy stone during the hallway to strike in his back of this head.  He falls down and passed away on the ground.

You broke into the room and saw they are arguing something. 

"No! Not on my watch!"

You interrupted them. You draw the sword, charing to the King.

"Oh no! Gawain!" He shouts but nobody answers.

You aim at it.
You have practiced it for thousands of nights in your sleep.
You will never miss it.
Your sword goes deep into his heart. 
Eyes widened, bloodshot and staring.
You looked staright into his eyes when the flame in his eyes start to fade away.
He is so ugly.
That is your first time seeing him this up close.
He died.

The sounds alarms the guards, you heard they are gathering outside. It's time to leave. You quickly run out of the room and head out to the shorted path out.

On the way out
you once looked back at the King's room for a second, 
Strangly,
You did not see grief in their eyes.

[[You safely get out and on the second day...]]







