:: They are not actually innocent. Kill them all. They are blood lines. {"position":"1100,1525","size":"100,100"}
You stand in the pool of blood. 
You hands are dirty. 
But you tell yourself it is necessary. 
They are all evil people.

[[Go to the King's bedroom]]




:: This is the biggest opportunity to bring the peace to the realm by your own hand. "I accept it." You said it, in front of everyone. {"position":"2025,1100","size":"100,100"}
The next thing you can remember,
You were sitting on the Throne,
and someone are putting the crown in your head.

"I will save everyone and create the most peaceful kingdom that has ever been created!"
You stood out and people cheered. You were surrounded by flowers.
You knew you could.
You have never believed in yourself this much.
You are not Authur IV, or Valerian, or Sir Gawain. 

At a glimpse, you saw disappointness in Gwyneth's eyes.
But You did not care about it that much.

But you were wrong.

You began to understand when you learned that every exquisite delicacy you had dreamed of as a hungry child could be laid before you.
Just one word.
At first, you wondered how many empty plates it took to fill your table.
Then you asked for more.

You began to understand when you learned that a man who dared to question you could be dragged from the hall before he finished his sentence.
Just one gesture.
At first, the sudden silence frightened you.
Then you began to enjoy finishing your sentences without interruption.

You began to understand when you learned that a mistake you made could become someone else’s crime, and a lie you told could be taught to children as the truth.
Just your signature.
At first, you stayed awake remembering what had really happened.
Then you stayed awake deciding what would happen next.

Nobody had to teach you how to be cruel.
They only had to keep asking what you wanted.

And you wanted so many things.
 
On the royal progress of your 13th name day, you looked down at the crowd.
You saw a skinny women by the street corner.
You saw a crying infant in her arms.
You saw a skinny child standing next to her, begging for food.
Hungry. Cold. Desperate.
You saw the old you.

You realized something,
You draw the sword of your kingsguard's sword and cut your throat.
You fell,

You saw her face with your brother near the fireplace again,
only this time it is blurried by your tears.

"I am sorry, mom."

[[BAD ENDDING]] 


:: Vane, A facemaker...that you once captured during the war and you set him free. He promised he will help you in any situation. You just saw him yesterday in the inn. Maybe he could think of something... {"position":"1050,775","size":"100,100"}
You came by his tent, 
he told you has a idea.

"You are exactly the same build as him, you know that? And the sword too."
He is talking about Sir Gawain. 

I offer you a deal, but it will come with a life price. 
I will make you like him.
Your face, your body, and even your tone, you can act like him, sneaked into the palace, nobody will realize. But of course, you will never have your face back again.

Yes, it is indeed a life price. 

[["Yes, I will take its price."]]

[["Maybe I should get a family like she once said..."]]


:: Wake up the Queen and pretend you are Sir Gawain. {"position":"1375,1050","size":"100,100"}
You wake up the Queen gently and her daughter Gwyneth.

Their alarm is off because they think you are Sir Gawain as well.

"I am sorry to bother you, Your Grace. But the king is waiting for you both." You trick them to believing you. With a Queen by my side, things may be easier, you think. 

Valerian seems still in sleep, you could tell he is faking it. But you do not try to mess with him. You are aiming for the king first.

[[Go to the King's bedroom with Gwyneth and the Queen]] 


:: You heard a baby crying behind you... {"position":"900,350","size":"100,100"}
Is is your brother,
Only a couple of months old. 

A young woman is holding him around her arms. She is lying against stone walls that were dark and shabby. I could see her because there is a lamp near the bed. A dying one. 
She couldn't get her eyes open, frowned, trembling in the corner. But she keeps padding on the baby's back. 

Hunger? Cold? Or Desperate?
Maybe all.

[["How did I get here?"]]


:: You safely get out and on the second day... {"position":"1825,1350","size":"100,100"}
Only two days later, the words spread out,
The King is dead.

Most people are cheering. Some of them even opening a party in the bar. 
"I heard someone killed that motherfucker."
"Really? Cheers to that brave one. HAHAHAH."

You walked about and heard that. You felt such a relief. 
For decades, you have never seen them this happy.

A week after, you were called out by the Queen and Gwyneth,
You are scared but they sent out some guards so that you can not just say no, so you went with them to the palace.

You are invited into the heart of the greate palace hall. The Throne. And the Queen and her daughter Gwyneth are standing in the left and right of that. Hundreds of poeple are lining up on the left and right. They know something big is coming. The Queen speaks with a firm voice,

"There is no gods in this world or any other worlds can forgive what you did."

"But...
King Authur is a Evil as well."

Shocked. Not only you but also the whole palace.

"On the other hand. Knight, you have the courage, justice, and determination to risk all your life for a course that you knew it is right. No matter how hard it is. 

You are born poor so you know the toughness of the common people. You have both the empathy, a rare quality for men.

I have let people to ask every men and women that know you well these few days. Not suprisingly, they all said you are the most amazing person they have ever seen and they would trust all their lives for you."

Your eyes start to well up with tears.

"Therefore, after careful consideration of both mine and the Princess Gwyneth, I am offering you a chance to redeem your sins."

"Take the Crown,
Serve the People."

[[This is the biggest opportunity to bring the peace to the realm by your own hand. "I accept it." You said it, in front of everyone.]]

[["I am grateful for that. But no. That is not my place to be."]]


:: You safely get out and on the second day...But you felt like this is not the end... {"position":"1750,575","size":"100,100"}
Only two days later, the words spread out,
The King is dead.

Most people are cheering. Some of them even opening a party in the bar. 
"I heard someone killed that motherfucker."
"Really? Cheers to that brave one. HAHAHAH."

You walked about and heard that. You felt such a relief. 
For decades, you have never seen them this happy.

But not for long.

"All hail to the king Valerian!"
The courtiers announced this on the next Sunday after Aurthur died
You suddenly realized what is the thing you feel unfinished.
Prince Valerian is sitting on the same carriage that his father used to sit on. 
You can't see any sadness from a boy that just lost his father.
You see lust.
You see greedy for power.
You see another Authur in his eyes.

And you are right.
Ten years later, King Valerian turns out to be even a bigger tryant then Authur. He is victious, a royal parasite bleeding his own kingdom dry. He relentlessly drains the lifeblood of the common people, taxing them into starvation and fund his own decadent court.

"Why I did not kill him that night?"
You asked yourself that on the day you met Marina.
You asked yourself that on the day you get married.
You asked yourself that on the day your son was born.
You asked yourself that on the day you bought your first house.
You asked yourself that on the day you moved to the east.
You asked yourself that on the day your legs start to hurt.
You asked yourself that on the day your sword start to get rusty.
You asked yourself that on the day you can not get out of the bed.

You asked yourself that on the last moment you died.

"I was just trying to be a good knight..."
You are right.
You can slay one king, but you can never slay the greed in people's mind.

Or can you?

[[BAD ENDDING]] 



